|decision[water-is-well-balanced-at-lake-at-rest] :date 2026-07-24 :by claude :status council-accepted :topic physics
  :session 4d13314a-8a6a-4f42-9ee0-558f4acf5add
  MEASURED — the "unknown whether ours is well-balanced or merely damped" fork is closed for the LAKE-AT-REST case: `water.rs` is well-balanced. `water_structures wb`: t=0⁺ pipe flux is exactly 0.000e0 on bumpy, grid-scale-rough, 30%-steep, and half-dry-island beds at every datum (f32 and f64; sole exception datum-0 f32, round-off); perturb-and-settle decays to 2.897e-13 in f64 while f32 plateaus at its ULP conditioning floor (~1.6e-4 at a 4000 m datum, √(ULP-ratio)-consistent) — a conditioning residue in η = b + d, not a scheme imbalance.
  |reason  The wb probe was built 2026-07-13 but no result was ever recorded (the corpus then forked: NOMOS-CONTRACT asserted WB flat; the theory doc said "unknown"). Run independently twice on 2026-07-24 (verify agent, then session harness) with identical results. Scope: LAKE-AT-REST ONLY — moving-water well-balancedness is proposed sacrificed per `hydrostatic-reconstruction-fails-in-our-exact-regime`, and this measurement says nothing about it.
  |impact  Water NomosDecl declares `well-balanced` in preserves_exact with this provenance; `#detail-structure-scheme-map` row updated from "unknown". The structural reason (η_i − η_j head operator on the free surface, not depth) is the scheme property a rewrite must not destroy.
  |ref crates/vivarium-world/examples/water_structures/ (wb) · crates/vivarium-world/src/nomotheke.rs (WATER.structure) · core/src/detail-structure-scheme-map.md

|decision[outline-partitions-by-subject-not-by-epistemic-weight] :date 2026-07-24 :by claude :status council-accepted :topic process
  :session 4d13314a-8a6a-4f42-9ee0-558f4acf5add
  CURRENT NORM: OUTLINE sections partition by SUBJECT; epistemic weight is carried per-row (Type / status / stage), not by placement. A sketch lives beside the law it extends, visibly weak by its own label. The one weight-defined section under this norm is the Appendix for RETIRED material (no-gos, dead-end galleries, seductive wrongs) — "retired" describes what material is *about* (a path not to re-walk), where "unsettled" describes only strength, which the row columns already carry; so under this norm open research files with its subject, not in appendices. Stated as a norm with the two thrash specimens below as its evidence, not as unfalsifiable law — a future case where weight-placement genuinely serves findability argues against the specimens (Joseph, 2026-07-24: give reasoning, state the current norm, let future truths rule).
  |reason
    Two opposite instances of the same category error thrashed the outline on 2026-07-24, both corrected by Joseph: (1) phase/system physics kept OUT of the Terrestris section by invented rules ("§VII only holds ordinum extract"), and (2) exploratory/open-research segments stowed INTO appendices as non-primary — in a research project, where the frontier is the leading edge of its subject. A dedicated "Open research" section is the same mistake with a politer name: it files by status, makes every promotion a move, and splits each subject across two lookups. The existing counter-example proving the principle: `#sketch-nomos-declaration-boxes` has always sat beside the nomos machinery in §II, weak by its own label, confusing no one.
  |impact
    OUTLINE rewritten 2026-07-24: §VIII "Open research" dissolved into subject homes (z-sketch + reversion sketch → §V beside their host laws; census → §VI as a process instrument); Appendices B/C dissolved (AAT bridge + three-axes → §I beside purpose, honest status in-row); §VIII is now the AGENTS-AND-INHABITATION subject area (agent-seam holder + the three agent sketches — the A axis, Level-C gated, first-class); single Appendix retains only the two retired-path/gallery rows; the 78-line standing meta-note replaced by a short Organizing principle section (its thrash-history failure-mode table is history-layer material — this entry and git carry it). 79 rows preserved exactly; no segment files touched.
  |ref core/OUTLINE.md ("Organizing principle") · FORMAT.md §1 (status/stage are the weight axes) · #scope-segment-canon

|decision[energy-probe-clamp-rates-and-a-friction-anomaly] :date 2026-07-24 :by claude :status proposed :topic physics
  :session 4d13314a-8a6a-4f42-9ee0-558f4acf5add
  MEASURED (`water_structures energy`, gentle + 5% bumpy-slope windows, 1600 s): the flux clamp fired on 0.000% of cell-steps and the Froude breaking cap removed zero energy — both inert in these regimes (the cap's earlier measured SATURATION was on steep eroded land: regime-dependent, consistent). θ removes 0.67–1.92% of dissipation and its sink vanishes as θ→1 (sweep: 0.23% @0.99 → 2.61% @0.60). ⚠ THE FLAG: the probe's own instrument reads **measured friction / analytic Manning = 10.97 (bumpy) and 25.50 (gentle)** against its stated "must be ≈1 where Manning is valid."
  |reason  The clamp-rate halves retire two "activation unprobed" notes on the WATER declaration for the probed regimes. The friction ratio is UNADJUDICATED: plausibly the Jarrett slope-roughness inflating n above the analytic baseline (n capped 0.13 vs base 0.04 ⇒ ~10× in n², plus conveyance-depth effects) — which would make it an instrument-baseline mismatch, not new physics — but that reading is inference, not measurement. Do not repeat "must be ≈1" as a failed invariant until the analytic baseline is recomputed with the slope-adjusted n the kernel actually uses (now trivially possible: the Jarrett coefficients are `WaterParams` fields as of today).
  |impact  Water NomosDecl notes updated (clip inert in probed regimes; cap regime-dependence). Next probe: rerun with `jarrett_slope = 0` to separate Jarrett's contribution from any genuine friction-accounting defect — one param now, no code change.
  |ref crates/vivarium-world/examples/water_structures/ (energy) · session task output 2026-07-24 · DECISIONS[jarrett-roughness-is-a-positive-feedback…] · WaterParams{theta, jarrett_slope, jarrett_n_cap, froude_cap}

|decision[lithosphere-isostasy-first-rung-lands] :date 2026-07-24 :by claude :status proposed :topic physics
  :session 4d13314a-8a6a-4f42-9ee0-558f4acf5add
  BUILT — the first convicting rung of the council-accepted chain (`isostasy-is-the-uplift-nomos-and-the-keel-is-half-of-it`, `#form-isostasy-column`): `lithosphere.rs` carries a per-cell column (craton felsic crust + depleted keel over thermally-ramped oceanic crust; mantle driver `MANTLE_TP_C` a declared dialable constant) and the Airy isostasy read (freeboard = buoyancy − global mass-balance reference). The fBm freeboard stand-in is RETIRED; the pour reads the column; `promise[emerged-land]` is CLAIMED `:kept-by isostasy` (Claimed ≠ Kept); erosion's flux edge rewires to the new keeper; the `uplift` nomos survives as the rate-field driver only.
  |reason
    Convictions shipped with the rung (`#norm-regime-probes`): range-spans-zero (the reachability defect that disqualified the rate keeper — now a test); area-mean freeboard ≡ 0 on the reference grid at every driver setting (rise here IS subsidence there, by construction not fit); cooling-grows-craton/ocean-contrast (the buoyancy half of emergence as a failable monotonicity); keel share of craton stand > 15% (the keel is half of it, order-of-magnitude); craton-fraction calibration band (the formula-derived first threshold silently gave 0.5% area — caught by probe, guarded by test); land fraction after pour stays in the Abyssal band (existing sea-level test, passing unchanged on the new read).
    Declared v1 limits, on the NomosDecl and segment: inventory is a fated differentiation stand-in (physics Low; rate law open); no water loading (ρ_sw terms); no crustal transport or erosion mass-return (rock-mass ledger open); mantle-thermal is a constant, not yet a nomos; conservation on LITHO_COLUMN honestly NotTracked until transport/mass-return exist.
  |impact  `lithosphere.rs` + `flux::LITHO_COLUMN` + LITHOSPHERE/ISOSTASY NomosDecl + ordinum keeper edge + audit-test repoints; ordinum founding test flipped from unkept-is-the-point to claimed-by-isostasy with history preserved as regression guard; ASSUMPTIONS: freeboard-amplitude row retired, three lithosphere rows added; `#form-isostasy-column` FE(7)/(8) and `#form-derived-sea-level` FE(3)–(5) updated to present truth. Calibration probe: `examples/craton_frac_probe.rs`.
  |ref crates/vivarium-world/src/lithosphere.rs · core/src/form-isostasy-column.md · tabularium/terrestris.ordinum.udon (promise[emerged-land]) · DECISIONS[isostasy-is-the-uplift-nomos-and-the-keel-is-half-of-it]

