|decision[emerged-land-record-predicate-built-and-two-clauses-convict] :date 2026-07-24 :by claude :status proposed :topic physics
  :session 8145183f-e9f3-4836-b4c8-edc86bed663e
  BUILT (council-fronted, `code-to-claim-wave-council-fronts-conservation-and-execution` clause 4) — the Record-style predicate probe for `promise[emerged-land]`, the Claimed→Kept INSTRUMENT (not a Kept verdict). `sea_level::emerged_land_verdict` adjudicates a per-seed Record against the early-continents survey §6 bands (land fraction 1.8-20%; peak subaerial stand <=2 km), split by what v1 can convict: HARD time-free clauses (land rises; fraction in band); a SOFT relief clause (measured on the pre-erosion surface, breach = amber flag not conviction); and the era-sharpening/timing clauses named NOT-YET-PREDICABLE (deep time does not run, so "per cycle" collapses to "per seed"). Probe: `examples/emerged_land_probe.rs`.
  |reason
    `#norm-probes-before-claims` rhythm: the predicate must exist before Kept can ever be marked, and building it decides nothing about the verdict. `#norm-probe-sensitivity` FE(2): two known-bads bracket the band and both fail — FLOOR = bathymetry-only water-world (0% land, fails land_rises/fraction); CEILING = a decreed sea level (old SEA_LEVEL_M-style datum) manufacturing forbidden land (seed 1 @ 3000 m -> 39.9%, fails fraction). So the green is a convicting green, not an insensitive one.
    MEASURED (level 8, seeds 0/1/7): land fraction 4.55 / 2.07 / 4.84 % (in-band, near the Flament MC-median floor); peak subaerial stand 2436 / 1724 / 2386 m. FINDING: seeds 0 and 7 AMBER-FLAG the ~2 km relief ceiling — isostatic freeboard alone OVER-STANDS the craton on the pre-erosion tectonic surface. Not a conviction of the promise (the strength limit + erosion mass-return that would trim it are declared-open, `#form-isostasy-column` FE(8)); it is an honest present-truth signal and a target for the rock-mass-ledger work.
  |impact  Predicate + probe + convicting tests in `sea_level.rs` / `examples/emerged_land_probe.rs`; `#form-isostasy-column` FE(6) now states the live predicate and the amber finding; `#detail-phase-abyssal` + `#form-derived-sea-level` + `#form-ordinum-governs-flux-web` + the ordinum `|predicate` line updated to present truth. `emerged-land` remains CLAIMED, NOT Kept — Kept awaits the temporal clauses (deep time) and a separate adjudication; not this entry's to grant.
