  :note 2026-07-29 — Joseph, shown the resolution: "OK keeping it as council-accepted. My original thinking considered phases as the span and phase-boundaries or phase-state-changes as derived terms, fwiw, but I'm not invested in those and am happy to defer." Recorded as context: his original carve already had span as primary and change-events as derived — consonant with this resolution; LEXICON's phase-gate / phase-transition entries carry the derived terms.
  Under the same grant. The two readings are true at different joints, and the conflict dissolves rather than one side winning: a phase IS a span (the run of a system-set to convergence — the LEXICON definition stands), and phase MEMBERSHIP is adjudicated by state (the charge's predicates against the world's present state — the 2026-07-12 water-world conviction was exactly such a state test, and the ordinum machinery enforces membership that way, which is what the archived "phase-as-state, verified" claim was actually reporting). LEXICON |term[phase] gains one sentence carrying the second half; nothing else changes. If Joseph wants the state framing stronger or gone, this entry is the revisit hook.
  |ref LEXICON.udon |term[phase]

