|decision[abf-quadrilateral-trap-does-not-apply-to-us] :date 2026-07-29 :by claude :status proposed :topic physics
  :session 91ddc84b-489e-4ce1-8898-02d4ad9993ad (opus structure strand)
  The Arnold-Boffi-Falk 2005 result (RT0 has no convergence of the divergence on non-affine quadrilaterals) is NOT the mechanism behind the grid report's measured two-point-flux inconsistency, and does not indict a finite-volume scheme on a cube-sphere quadtree. Three separations, one read-primary and two measured: (1) ABF's statement is about representing the divergence GIVEN exact fluxes; ours is about the flux itself. (2) The measured defect is present on a parallelogram lattice where ABF is provably absent (46% error, order -> 0; orthogonal control clean at 2.000). (3) ABF's non-convergence requires a mesh sequence of FIXED cell shape (measured flat delta/h = 6.35e-1 on their own trapezoid mesh) whereas a cube-sphere quadtree is asymptotically affine (delta/h -> 0 at order 1.998). Bochev-Ridzal's rehabilitation does exempt an FV divergence (the natural mimetic divergence IS the FV divergence) but the exemption is no news, not good news: it removes an obstacle never on our path. The check's real value: it stopped a false attribution that would have retired a live defect by citation. Retires survey §9 "Resolve before B1" items 1-2.
  |ref msc/agent-briefs/2026-07-29-gcl-and-abf-checks.md · crates/vivarium-world/examples/gcl_abf_probe.rs · relata: arnold-2005-quadhdiv (read primary §1, §8) · msc/research-structure-preserving/README.md §4.8

|decision[the-discrete-gcl-is-a-spec-not-a-defect] :date 2026-07-29 :by claude :status proposed :topic physics
  :session 91ddc84b-489e-4ce1-8898-02d4ad9993ad (opus structure strand)
  The discrete geometric conservation law is not violated by our staggered-FV metric set because THERE IS NO staggered-FV metric set: measure.rs carries areas, centres, centre-distances and no edge length, edge normal, or arm; the flux-form kernel (water.rs) runs a single scalar cell_m for every length and area — a uniform-Cartesian stand-in that fails free-stream preservation at O(1), not decaying (measured, known-bad arm). The identity itself is derived and EXACT for our grid: cube-sphere cell edges are great-circle arcs whose outward in-surface normal is the arc's constant pole, so Sum_e L_e p_e + 2*Int_K r dOmega = 0 — verified ~1e-15 against independent quadrature at four levels; the free-stream half telescopes combinatorially (6e-16). So the GCL becomes a BUILD-TIME ACCEPTANCE TEST for the four unbuilt edge quantities, not a diagnostic of existing ones. Retires survey §10's second open.
  |ref msc/agent-briefs/2026-07-29-gcl-and-abf-checks.md · crates/vivarium-world/examples/gcl_abf_probe.rs · msc/research-structure-preserving/README.md §4.9

|decision[the-two-point-flux-defect-is-a-panel-seam-defect] :date 2026-07-29 :by claude :status proposed :topic physics
  :session 91ddc84b-489e-4ce1-8898-02d4ad993ad (opus structure strand; mispredicted pre-registration — the agent expected pre-asymptotic, measured persistent to N=256 — and the resolution is the finding)
  On the equiangular cube-sphere the measured order -0.50 of the two-point flux is carried ~99.5% by the single ring of cells touching a cube-panel seam: local relative error there is O(1/h), doubling per rung (2.5 -> 5.1 -> 10.3 -> 20.6), while every interior band CONVERGES (~+0.45) and the face interior plateaus. Seam-cell edge lengths, distances, skew are within 2% of interior; only non-orthogonality is elevated (29.7 vs 11.3 deg) and that is O(1), insufficient alone. The clean -0.5 is arithmetic: O(1/h) error on a codimension-1 set contributes h^{-1/2} to a 2-D L2 norm. CONSEQUENCE: any scheme keeping a two-point flux across a panel seam has a divergent operator there regardless of bulk behaviour — and this needs NO hanging node; it is present on conforming same-level seams. Sharpens grid report §5.2's [D] mechanism (three controls fail to reproduce its global account); does not conflict with its corner-defect refutation (different split). Decisive next test, named: freeze the metric across a band either side of a seam and see whether the growth vanishes. Reproduced by the orchestrator before landing (tpfa_ladder, N=32..256).
  |ref msc/agent-briefs/2026-07-29-gcl-and-abf-checks.md · crates/vivarium-world/examples/tpfa_ladder.rs · ref/research/grid-comparison-report.md §5.2

|decision[fe6c-reconstruction-is-cube-safe-but-the-diagonal-kill-alone-is-cheaper] :date 2026-07-29 :by claude :status proposed :topic physics
  :session 91ddc84b-489e-4ce1-8898-02d4ad9993ad (opus router strand; pre-registered predictions, P2 confirmed, P4/P5/P6 refuted)
  FE(6)(c)'s Coatleven flux-vector reconstruction is BUILT and PRICED on the receiver/incision tree (`examples/router_fe6c.rs`, 8 seeds, null-pair-controlled). Three present truths. (1) The belief FE(8) recorded as unmeasured is now measured and TRUE: the principled remedy is ~3x more cube-safe than the naive-D4 strawman (RMS mean-CUBE 0.055 vs 0.177; |CUBE| < 0.5*|CUBE(EdgeFull)| at every threshold). The strawman's +0.07..+0.26 swing was a property of the D4 tree's four fixed azimuths, not of removing diagonals. (2) It buys NOTHING over the cheapest arm: kill the diagonals, weight faces by transmissivity |sigma|*drop/d, keep the LIVE D8 tree — RMS-CUBE 0.033, the most cube-safe arm measured, no reconstruction and no gradient operator. So channel orientation is no longer an argument for building FE(6c); the reconstruction's real justification (q~_K has no mesh-independent limit, Coatleven SS2.4) is a consistency claim CUBE does not measure. (3) The MAGNITUDE half is unpriced and its arm is confounded: consuming ||Q_K||*sqrt(A_K) gives RMS-CUBE 0.162 (strawman-sized), but ||Q|| is a SPECIFIC catchment area fed to a stream-power law with k_dt unchanged — a fair test restates stream power in specific-catchment-area form with re-tuned erodibility, and has not been run. Affordability (census open): ANSWERED, 1.06x live wall-time. Halo (census open): halo 2, DERIVED not measured, and it is the price of the RECONSTRUCTION not of the LSQ gradient. Standing s_K=0 limit: carved out and measured INERT here (fill-raised cells 0.0-0.2%; carve-out moves CUBE < 0.003) — the limit is real but bites on endorheic configurations, not on an uplifting dome with base-level sinks; name that condition when next invoking it.
  |ref msc/spike-router-fe6c/RESULTS.md · msc/spike-router-fe6c/PREDICTIONS.md · crates/vivarium-world/examples/router_fe6c.rs · msc/agent-briefs/2026-07-29-router-fe6c-pricing.md

|decision[the-cube-metric-now-has-a-null-control-and-the-prior-terrain-was-a-paraboloid] :date 2026-07-29 :by claude :status proposed :topic process
  :session 91ddc84b-489e-4ce1-8898-02d4ad9993ad (opus router strand)
  Two validity findings that precede every CUBE number ever reported, including the 2026-07-24 pricing. (1) THE METRIC HAD NO NULL CONTROL. CUBE is a difference of differences of a fraction over a few thousand cells and nothing established what it returns when there is nothing to find. Added: an 8-seed sweep giving every value a sd, and a NULL PAIR — CUBE computed over two D4-SYMMETRIC footprints (face centres on ZPos and XPos), where the cube-locked term vanishes by symmetry. Every arm comes back consistent with zero (|mean| <= 0.047 against sd 0.01-0.10). The metric passes, for the first time, and the floor is set: RMS-CUBE below ~0.01-0.03 is not distinguishable from nothing. (2) THE PRIOR HARNESS'S TERRAIN WAS A BARE ANALYTIC PARABOLOID. `router_pricing.rs::terrain` documents "broad paraboloid + real band-limited prior detail (natural channel seeding)"; the detail term is `initial_topography_m(seed,c,c.level()) - initial_topography_m(seed,c,level)` and the harness builds every cell AT `level`, so it is IDENTICALLY ZERO. Worse, seed 0 — the seed that experiment used — has measured zero spectral content between levels 14 and 19, so it carries no relief at any band. Channels therefore formed on a near-radially-symmetric dome where the router's own lattice bias is close to the only symmetry-breaking present: the same species of hazard as the face-centre cone null test (#norm-probe-sensitivity), which this project has already been bitten by once. Corrected here (band level-5..level, seeds 1-8). CONSEQUENCE, and it is why this is not a footnote: on the paraboloid the FE(6d) arm told the OPPOSITE story from real terrain — a clean "the corrected gradient is what buys cube-safety" (z=22) that dissolves once the terrain has relief. That claim would have shipped. The strawman's CUBE band nevertheless replicates on corrected terrain (+0.073/+0.160/+0.250 vs +0.070/+0.148/+0.255), so FE(8)'s conclusion survives; its terrain description does not.
  |ref msc/spike-router-fe6c/RESULTS.md · crates/vivarium-world/examples/router_fe6c.rs · crates/vivarium-world/examples/router_pricing.rs · .super-archive/from-msc/spike-router-pricing/RESULTS.md

|decision[cell-solid-angle-loses-relative-precision-as-the-level-refines] :date 2026-07-29 :by claude :status proposed :topic architecture
  :session 91ddc84b-489e-4ce1-8898-02d4ad9993ad (opus router strand; found incidentally, gate-driven)
  `measure::cell_solid_angle` evaluates F(u1,v1)-F(u1,v0)-F(u0,v1)+F(u0,v0) with F = atan(XY/sqrt(1+X^2+Y^2)). The four terms are O(1) and converge on each other as the cell shrinks, so the RELATIVE cancellation error grows like 4^level. Measured against the cancellation-free Van Oosterom-Strackee form (probe: `examples/solid_angle_precision.rs`): median/max relative error 5.3e-10/4.7e-9 at L13, 1.6e-6/2.9e-5 at L19, 3.2e-5/4.9e-4 at L21, 4.1e-4/5.4e-3 at L23, 5.5e-3/6.8e-2 at L25 (MAX_LEVEL). This is a LIVE-KERNEL function: `cell_area_m2` is the per-cell runoff in `erosion::accumulate_drainage` and the volume in `deposit`, and it REPLACED uniform cell_m^2 precisely because per-cell area accuracy was shown to matter (#obs-cube-locked-kernel-bias, +17.8% area-weighted bias). Harmless at L19; at the walk-scale tiers the repo already contemplates it carries 0.04%-0.5% median per-cell noise that is spatially HIGH-FREQUENCY — the shape that reads as sub-grid texture rather than as a numerical floor. Fix is a drop-in (VOS on the four corners; same inputs, no new dependency, no behaviour change above L16). NOT LANDED: a src/ edit re-keys every world under every cohort (#form-complete-content-addressed-key) and sibling agents shared the store. Joseph's or the orchestrator's call when to take the re-key.
  |ref crates/vivarium-world/examples/solid_angle_precision.rs · crates/vivarium-world/src/measure.rs · msc/spike-router-fe6c/RESULTS.md

|decision[cell-solid-angle-now-uses-a-difference-formed-spherical-excess] :date 2026-07-29 :by claude :status proposed :topic architecture :supersedes cell-solid-angle-loses-relative-precision-as-the-level-refines
  :session 91ddc84b-489e-4ce1-8898-02d4ad9993ad (opus router strand; landed under Joseph's explicit re-key grant)
  GRANT (Joseph, 2026-07-29, verbatim): "Don't worry about rekeying -- get the truth in place :-) Let the cache worry about the cache." Landed accordingly; the superseded entry had parked the fix over store invalidation.
  `measure::cell_solid_angle` now computes the cell's spherical excess as two Van Oosterom-Strackee triangles with the triple product formed as `a.((b-a)x(c-a))` -- algebraically identical to `a.(bxc)` but built from DIFFERENCES of nearby corner vectors. The retired closed form (four O(1) arctangents whose difference is the tiny solid angle) lost relative precision as 4^level.
  ⚠ CORRECTION TO THE SUPERSEDED ENTRY, and it is the substantive part: that entry named "VOS on the four corners" as the drop-in fix. Measured against a real reference, the NAIVE VOS form degrades as 4^level TOO -- 1.8e-3 at L25 -- only ~7x better than the form it replaces. The superseded entry would have bought a factor of 7 while claiming a factor of a million. The DIFFERENCE REFORMULATION is the load-bearing part. The error was methodological: the original probe used naive VOS AS its reference, so it could measure a disagreement but could not attribute it. The reference now is tensor Gauss-Legendre on the Jacobian -- a sum of POSITIVE terms times an exactly-representable cell size, cancellation-free by shape, self-converged to ~2e-16 (reported in the probe, which is what licenses it as truth).
  MEASURED, relative to that reference: legacy -4.8e-10 (L13) / -3.0e-6 (L19) / +2.9e-4 (L23) / -1.3e-2 (L25); naive VOS -3.1e-11 / -5.9e-7 / +6.2e-5 / +1.8e-3; LIVE (landed) -5.6e-13 / -1.9e-11 / -2.9e-10 / -4.0e-10 -- FLAT from L16 on, six to seven orders better, no longer 4^level. Coarse levels where the old form was healthy are unchanged to rounding (L4 delta 3e-16). The value change at any level is exactly the old error at that level, which is what makes this a precision fix and not a physics change.
  INDEPENDENT CORROBORATION: an unrelated gate in `examples/router_fe6c.rs` -- max |A_spherical/A_planar - 1| at L19, measuring the genuine sphericity of the cell against the tangent-plane quad -- moved 4.44e-5 -> 5.44e-8 across this change, exactly as the diagnosis predicted. Different file, different quantity, predicted direction and magnitude.
  RE-KEY: every stored world cohort is invalidated by design (SRC_HASH; `#form-complete-content-addressed-key`). Accepted cost, per the grant above. `bin/check` green (180 lib + 3 cli_admission + decision-refs + null-space gate + determinism clippy). The FE(6c) pricing was re-run across the change and every conclusion and the whole arm ordering survive (RMS-CUBE shifts < 0.007). The probe carries a hard GUARD (worst |live/quad - 1| over L13..L25 < 1e-8, measured 2.5e-9) so a future simplification back to a cancelling form fails loudly rather than silently inside a landscape.
  |ref crates/vivarium-world/src/measure.rs · crates/vivarium-world/examples/solid_angle_precision.rs · msc/spike-router-fe6c/RESULTS.md · msc/agent-briefs/2026-07-29-router-fe6c-pricing.md
